\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the residual hybrid-diffusion policy. \textbf  {(a)} Inference. The frozen SmolVLA encodes the two camera images, the instruction and the robot state in a single prefix pass. Its hidden states are mean-pooled into the semantic feature $z$, and its key--value cache drives SmolVLA's own action expert, which samples the base action chunk $a^{b}$. The trainable head (green) samples a residual chunk $\hat  r$ conditioned on both $z$ and $a^{b}$. The first action of $a^{b}+\alpha \hat  r$ is un-normalised, clipped and executed, and the procedure repeats on the next observation. \textbf  {(b)} Training. Demonstration states are replayed in the simulator and passed once through the frozen model to build a cache of features, base-action samples and demonstrated actions; the head is then trained on the cache with a flow-matching loss on the residual $a^{\star }-a^{b}$. Grey: frozen; green: trainable; orange: data and environment.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{3}{}{}{}}
