\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Architecture of the residual flow head $v_\theta $. The noisy residual chunk is flattened and projected to a 512-D hidden vector $h$. Flow time, the semantic feature and the base action chunk are embedded separately and summed into one conditioning vector $e$, which modulates each of six residual blocks through a feature-wise scale $\gamma (e)$ and shift $\beta (e)$. The output is the predicted velocity for all 16 steps of the chunk.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:head}{{2}{4}{}{}{}}
